--
--   Description
--
-- This tests the receive functionality for accepting maximum sized 
-- frames in both normal gigabit and burst gigabit operation. 
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- · Ensures that the GEM will only accept a frame up to the maximum size 
--     of 1518 bytes in both normal and burst gigabit operation.  
-- · Ensure that the GEM can also accept maximum sized frames of 1522 bytes 
--     when configured properly in both normal and burst gigabit operation.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- 
-- Receiving Long Frames (1518 bytes) in Normal Gigabit operation
-- 10. Initialise the GEM for gigabit operation.
-- 11. Receive a frame that is 1519 bytes long.
-- 12. Receive a frame that is 1518 bytes long.
-- 13. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure 
--         that the above operations were handled properly.
-- 
-- Receiving Long Frames (1536 bytes) in Normal Gigabit operation
-- 14. Enable the GEM to receive frames which are 1522 bytes long.
-- 15. Receive a frame that is 1522 bytes long.
-- 16. Receive a frame that is 1523 bytes long.
-- 17. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure 
--         that the above operations were handled properly.
-- 
-- Receiving Long Frames (1518 bytes) in Burst Gigabit mode
-- 18. In burst mode, receive a frame that is the maximum frame size 
--         and then receive a second frame that is one byte over the 
--         maximum frame size..
-- 19. In burst mode, receive two frames of maximum frame size.
-- 20. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure 
--         that the above operations were handled properly.
-- 
-- Receiving Long Frames (1536 bytes) in Burst Gigabit mode
-- 21. Initialise the GEM to receive 1536 byte long frames.
-- 22. In burst mode, receive a frame that is 1536 bytes and then 
--         receive a second frame that is one byte over 1536 bytes.
-- 23. In burst mode, receive two frames that are 1536 bytes.
-- 24. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure 
--         that the above operations were handled properly.
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      04 00080401  -- indicate 1G operation
apbrd      04 00080401  -- verify write to speed register..
apbrd      20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register and trigger reception of frame
apbwr      88 12345678  -- set the local address register to
apbwr      8c 00001111  --   ensure the incoming frame is recieved

